    {
      "record_id": "switch:locres:set-02:ST_SubEv_Dng08Gro43_Theme:SubEv_Dng08Gro43_Theme_015:566a080f",
      "source": {
        "set": "set-02",
        "namespace": "ST_SubEv_Dng08Gro43_Theme",
        "key": "SubEv_Dng08Gro43_Theme_015",
        "jp_record_id": "switch:locres:set-02:ST_SubEv_Dng08Gro43_Theme:SubEv_Dng08Gro43_Theme_015:566a080f",
        "official_en_record_id": "switch:locres:set-02:ST_SubEv_Dng08Gro43_Theme:SubEv_Dng08Gro43_Theme_015:566a080f",
        "jp_sha256": "b725f21e693a3392416b41937efd33c669c0c83d290dc39e22e681fc73850862",
        "official_en_sha256": "03ff65d6d681d632a5d7ff6fefaff2b4145344cc8cbde61fdb512b0ecd53093c"
      },
      "text": {
        "jp": "猛き者は剣をふるい、智ある者は魔法に通ず。\r\n賢者ならば、敵を見て、これを使い分けよ",
        "official_en": "The mighty wield blades, the clever command magic. The wise must choose well—or face an end most tragic.",
        "real_en": "The fierce wield swords, the learned use magic. A sage watches the enemy and chooses which to use."
      },
